Well, I've changed my mind.

When I first started playing this game, I
thought I would never play humans.  I figured
infravision was a well-nigh insurmountable
advantage for the other races. Not to
mention sleep resistance, or inherent
poison resistance, or...

But after 13 ascensions I've changed my mind.
Those are all useful in the early game, but
all those advantages dry up as the human
player finds telepathy and starts eating
monster corpses. By the mid-game, the
advantages of the starting races are gone
but the weaknesses remain ... which typically
results in a lower hit point total, or a lower
strength, or a lower constitution, or a lower int.

Only the human has the capacity to reach
18/99 and 18 in all stats.  Thus, I find that
I really do prefer the human over any other
available race. It starts off weaker than the
others, but the weaknesses fade over time
and the strengths come out.

Is that other people's experience as well? or
is there a particular race you have come to
prefer?

